      en: "Tidra Island is a small uninhabited island within Banc d'Arguin National Park, covering 5 km². It is one of the most important nesting sites in West Africa for seabirds such as pelicans, flamingos, and terns. The island consists of sand dunes and beaches. Access is limited to researchers and park staff to minimize disturbance. The surrounding shallow waters are rich in fish, providing food for the birds.",
